 suffering with painful trachoma. Her mother, Lupula, wished for her daughter to be able to see and enjoy the world around her.\",\"credit\":\"Stuart Tibaweswa\"},{\"image\":{\"ID\":120757,\"id\":120757,\"title\":\"2506_Sightsavers_Sarah-and-her-mum\",\"filename\":\"2506_Sightsavers_Sarah-and-her-mum.png\",\"filesize\":2415887,\"url\":\"\\/wp-content\\/uploads\\/2026\\/02\\/2506_Sightsavers_Sarah-and-her-mum.png\",\"link\":\"https:\\/\\/en.sightsavers.co\\/appeals\\/make-extraordinary-change\\/attachment\\/2506_sightsavers_sarah-and-her-mum-2\\/\",\"alt\":\"Lupula holds her daughter Sarah outside. She looks off into the distance smiling widely.\",\"author\":\"202\",\"description\":\"\",\"caption\":\"\",\"name\":\"2506_sightsavers_sarah-and-her-mum-2\",\"status\":\"inherit\",\"uploaded_to\":120635,\"date\":\"2026-02-09 16:43:41\",\"modified\":\"2026-02-09 16:43:58\",\"menu_order\":0,\"mime_type\":\"image\\/png\",\"type\":\"image\",\"subtype\":\"png\",\"icon\":\"https:\\/\\/en.sightsavers.co\\/wp-includes\\/images\\/media\\/default.png\",\"width\":1500,\"height\":843,\"sizes\":{\"thumbnail\":\"https:\\/\\/en.sightsavers.co\\/wp-content\\/uploads\\/2026\\/02\\/2506_Sightsavers_Sarah-and-her-mum-150x150.png\",\"thumbnail-width\":150,\"thumbnail-height\":150,\"medium\":\"https:\\/\\/en.sightsavers.co\\/wp-content\\/uploads\\/2026\\/02\\/2506_Sightsavers_Sarah-and-her-mum-300x169.png\",\"medium-width\":300,\"medium-height\":169,\"medium_large\":\"https:\\/\\/en.sightsavers.co\\/wp-content\\/uploads\\/2026\\/02\\/2506_Sightsavers_Sarah-and-her-mum-768x432.png\",\"medium_large-width\":768,\"medium_large-height\":432,\"large\":\"https:\\/\\/en.sightsavers.co\\/wp-content\\/uploads\\/2026\\/02\\/2506_Sightsavers_Sarah-and-her-mum-1024x575.png\",\"large-width\":1024,\"large-height\":575,\"1536x1536\":\"https:\\/\\/en.sightsavers.co\\/wp-content\\/uploads\\/2026\\/02\\/2506_Sightsavers_Sarah-and-her-mum.png\",\"1536x1536-width\":1500,\"1536x1536-height\":843,\"2048x2048\":\"https:\\/\\/en.sightsavers.co\\/wp-content\\/uploads\\/2026\\/02\\/2506_Sightsavers_Sarah-and-her-mum.png\",\"2048x2048-width\":1500,\"2048x2048-height\":843,\"hero\":\"https:\\/\\/en.sightsavers.co\\/wp-content\\/uploads\\/2026\\/02\\/2506_Sightsavers_Sarah-and-her-mum-1400x788.png\",\"hero-width\":1400,\"hero-height\":788,\"teaser\":\"https:\\/\\/en.sightsavers.co\\/wp-content\\/uploads\\/2026\\/02\\/2506_Sightsavers_Sarah-and-her-mum-580x326.png\",\"teaser-width\":580,\"teaser-height\":326,\"cta\":\"https:\\/\\/en.sightsavers.co\\/wp-content\\/uploads\\/2026\\/02\\/2506_Sightsavers_Sarah-and-her-mum-660x370.png\",\"cta-width\":660,\"cta-height\":370}},\"caption\":\"Thankfully, Sarah received antibiotics to treat her trachoma infection as part of mass drug administrations in her village in Zambia. \",\"credit\":\"Stuart Tibaweswa\"}]' data-theme-link=\"/wp-content/themes/theme//assets/\" id=\"image-gallery_1719004835\"></div>\n</div>"
